        "title": "History of Comics as a Form",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "WILLIAM HOGARTH (1697-1764)\n  \"A Rake's Progress\" (1735): 8 paintings in sequence\n  \"Marriage A-la-Mode\" (1743-45): 6 paintings\n  Designed as series to be read sequentially\n  Moral satire through visual narrative\n  Engraved and sold widely: mass distribution of sequential narrative\n  McCloud cites Hogarth as foundational precursor"
    },
    {
      "id": "01-HISTORY-FORM.md#008",
