        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "History of Comics as a Form",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "RODOLPHE TOPFFER (1799-1846) -- THE REAL ORIGIN POINT\n  Swiss cartoonist and educator\n  \"Histoire de Mr. Jabot\" (1827, published 1833)\n  \"Dr. Festus\" (1829); \"Monsieur Cryptogame\" (1830)\n  WHAT HE INVENTED:\n  - Panels with clear borders\n  - Captions below images\n  - Simple, expressive line drawing\n  - Narrative sequence driven by image, not text\n  Goethe praised his work; Topffer = legitimate precursor of modern comics\n  His albums were widely pirated in US and Europe (first comics piracy)\n```"
    },
