      "text": "```\nRICHARD OUTCAULT'S \"YELLOW KID\" (1895)\n  New York World (Pulitzer); then New York Journal (Hearst)\n  Character: bald child in yellow nightshirt; urban slum setting\n  Was this the first comic strip?\n  Arguments for: speech balloon (in color; character's nightshirt)\n                 sequential if read across runs\n  Arguments against: early strips were single images, not panels"
    },
    {
      "id": "01-HISTORY-FORM.md#013",
      "path": [
        "01-HISTORY-FORM.md"
