      "text": "KRAZY KAT (George Herriman, 1913-1944)\n  New York Evening Journal\n  About: Kat loves Ignatz Mouse; Ignatz throws bricks at Kat;\n         Officer Pupp tries to arrest Ignatz; Kat loves being hit\n  Significance: Language play, poetry, surrealism; racial ambiguity\n               E.E. Cummings wrote an essay praising it\n               Gilbert Seldes called it the greatest American art form\n               Ran until Herriman's death; Hearst personally kept it running\n               despite limited circulation"
